SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Summary: WINENCPU: cap the number of processors reported to programs
Category: cpu
Kind: feature
Origin: crossover (ported here)
  Version: 25.1.1
  CW-Hacks: 24711
  URL: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-25.1.1.tar.gz
  Files: dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
  Changes: SystemProcessorPerformanceInformation's macOS branch also
    returns no more entries than the capped count (CX's returned one per
    real processor when the buffer had room)
  Note: Sikarugir 10.0_8 ships it: ntdll.so has "WINENCPU", "Restricting
    number of processors to %ld."
Upstream: no
Why: Off unless WINENCPU is set. WINENCPU=<n>, with n at least 1 and below
 the Mac's logical processor count, makes Wine report n processors (macOS
 only): in GetSystemInfo, GetActiveProcessorCount, the affinity masks, the
 processor registry keys, the logical processor information (packages and
 cores clamped to n, cache sharing kept consistent) and the processor
 performance information. For programs that break with many cores.
 Threads still run on every core.
Programs: none known; programs that size thread pools or per-core buffers
 from the processor count and fail with many cores
Enable: env WINENCPU=<n> (per process; 1 <= n < the Mac's logical processor count)
Messages: "Restricting number of processors to %ld." (WARN, shown only
 with WINEDEBUG=warn+ntdll)
Uncertain: which program CrossOver added it for (CW HACK 24711).
Status: 10.0: 2026-11-26: SystemProcessorPerformanceInformation capped too
 10.0: 2026-11-26: quick builds 20261126T013940 and T024442 (macOS 26.7.2,
 M1 Max): smoke and the regression suite passed

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
@@ -1217,6 +1217,12 @@ static NTSTATUS create_logical_proc_info(void)
     size = sizeof(cores_no);
     if (sysctlbyname("hw.physicalcpu", &cores_no, &size, NULL, 0))
         cores_no = lcpu_no;
+
+    /* CW HACK 24711: allow restricting the number of processors through an environment variable.
+     * Don't report more packages or physical cores than logical cores.
+     */
+    pkgs_no = MIN(pkgs_no, lcpu_no);
+    cores_no = MIN(cores_no, lcpu_no);
 
     TRACE("%u logical CPUs from %u physical cores across %u packages\n",
             lcpu_no, cores_no, pkgs_no);
@@ -1280,6 +1286,14 @@ static NTSTATUS create_logical_proc_info(void)
         cache_sharing[4] = cache_sharing[3];
         cache_sharing[3] = cache_sharing[2];
         cache_sharing[2] = cache_sharing[1];
+
+        /* CW HACK 24711: allow restricting the number of processors through an environment variable
+         * The number of processors (logical cores) needs to be divisible by the number of logical
+         * cores sharing a cache.
+         */
+        if (cache_sharing[4] && (lcpu_no % cache_sharing[4])) cache_sharing[4] = 1;
+        if (cache_sharing[3] && (lcpu_no % cache_sharing[3])) cache_sharing[3] = 1;
+        if (cache_sharing[2] && (lcpu_no % cache_sharing[2])) cache_sharing[2] = 1;
     }
 
     for(p = 0; p < pkgs_no; ++p)
@@ -1400,7 +1414,24 @@ void init_cpu_info(void)
 #else
     num = 1;
     FIXME("Detecting the number of processors is not supported.\n");
+#endif
+
+#if defined(__APPLE__)
+    /* CW HACK 24711: allow restricting the number of processors through an environment variable */
+    {
+        const char *ncpu = getenv("WINENCPU");
+        if (ncpu)
+        {
+            long num_override = atoi(ncpu);
+            if (num_override > 0 && num_override < num)
+            {
+                num = num_override;
+                WARN("Restricting number of processors to %ld.\n", num);
+            }
+        }
+    }
 #endif
+
     peb->NumberOfProcessors = cpu_info.MaximumProcessors = num;
     get_cpuinfo( &cpu_info );
     TRACE( "<- CPU arch %d, level %d, rev %d, features 0x%x\n",
@@ -3055,7 +3086,8 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtQuerySystemInformation( SYSTEM_INFOR
                                      &info_count) == 0)
             {
                 int i;
-                cpus = min(cpus,out_cpus);
+                /* WINENCPU: no more entries than the processors reported */
+                cpus = min( min( cpus, out_cpus ), peb->NumberOfProcessors );
                 for (i = 0; i < cpus; i++)
                 {
                     sppi[i].IdleTime.QuadPart = pinfo[i].cpu_ticks[CPU_STATE_IDLE];
